-## Subtopics
-
-### Snap Marching Cubes
-Aligns vertices to grid nodes to reduce mesh complexity. Choose when topological precision is less critical than vertex count. [Snap Marching Cubes](2181-snap-marching-cubes.md)
-
-### Hermite Dual Marching Cubes
-Uses Hermite interpolation for smoother surfaces. Choose when surface smoothness is paramount. [Hermite Dual Marching Cubes](2197-hermite-dual-marching-cubes.md)
-
-### SDF to PLY Conversion
-Converts Signed Distance Fields directly to PLY format. Choose when working with SDFs and needing a specific output format. [SDF to PLY Conversion](2343-sdf-to-ply-conversion.md)
-
-### CPU Immediate Mode Marching Cubes
-Renders triangles immediately without storing them. Choose for real-time visualization with minimal memory. [CPU Immediate Mode Marching Cubes](2463-cpu-immediate-mode-marching-cubes.md)
-
-### Marching Cubes Triangulation
-Focuses on the triangulation step. Choose when the lookup table configuration is already handled. [Marching Cubes Triangulation](3682-marching-cubes-triangulation.md)
-
-### Simplified Marching Cubes
-Reduces the number of cases. Choose for faster processing with acceptable topological variations. [Simplified Marching Cubes](3759-simplified-marching-cubes.md)
-
-### Preprocessed Marching Cubes
-Precomputes data for faster extraction. Choose when the volume is static and extraction is frequent. [Preprocessed Marching Cubes](3765-preprocessed-marching-cubes.md)
-
-### Sparse Marching Cubes
-Optimizes for sparse data. Choose when the volume has large empty regions. [Sparse Marching Cubes](3825-sparse-marching-cubes.md)
-
-### Marching Cubes with Narrow-Band Filtering
-Filters the volume before extraction. Choose when noise reduction is needed. [Marching Cubes with Narrow-Band Filtering](3826-marching-cubes-with-narrow-band-filtering.md)
-
-### Marching Cubes with QEF Vertex Optimization
-Optimizes vertex positions using Quadratic Error Functions. Choose for higher geometric accuracy. [Marching Cubes with QEF Vertex Optimization](3831-marching-cubes-with-qef-vertex-optimization.md)
-
-### Modified Marching Cubes with Triangle Decimation
-Reduces triangle count post-extraction. Choose for lower polygon count. [Modified Marching Cubes with Triangle Decimation](3903-modified-marching-cubes-with-triangle-decimation.md)
-
-### GPU Acceleration and Parallel Pipelines
-Uses GPU for parallel processing. Choose for high performance on large datasets. [GPU Acceleration and Parallel Pipelines](4136-gpu-acceleration-and-parallel-pipelines.md)
-
-### Marching Cubes Vertex List Generation
-Generates a list of unique vertices. Choose when vertex sharing is needed but not automatic. [Marching Cubes Vertex List Generation](4447-marching-cubes-vertex-list-generation.md)
-
-### Lookup Table and Configuration
-Defines the MC lookup table. Choose when customizing the triangulation cases. [Lookup Table and Configuration](4978-lookup-table-and-configuration.md)
-
-### Marching Cubes with Disjoint Patch Decomposition
-Decomposes the volume into patches. Choose for distributed processing. [Marching Cubes with Disjoint Patch Decomposition](5004-marching-cubes-with-disjoint-patch-decomposition.md)
-
-### Transvoxel
-Multi-resolution isosurface extraction. Choose for adaptive resolution. [Transvoxel](6277-transvoxel.md)
-
-### Marching Tetrahedra
-Uses tetrahedra instead of cubes. Choose to avoid ambiguous cases. [Marching Tetrahedra](6534-marching-tetrahedra.md)
-
 ## Operating characteristics
 - **Time Complexity:** $O(N)$ where $N$ is the number of cells, assuming hash table operations are $O(1)$ on average [G].
-- **Memory Complexity:** $O(S)$ where $S$ is the size of the isosurface (number of unique vertices), plus $O(V_{slice})$ for the streaming buffer. This is significantly lower than storing the entire volume if the volume is much larger than the surface [G].
+- **Memory Complexity:** $O(S)$ where $S$ is the size of the isosurface (number of unique vertices), plus $O(V_{slice})$ for the streaming buffer [G].
 - **Measured Performance:** Allows processing of extremely large datasets that would otherwise exceed memory limits [S2].
 - **Scaling:** Scales well with dataset size as only a small portion of the volume is in memory at any time [S2].
